path stale-and-pin
kind flow
author ai
group map
note What happens when code under a step changes. Every anchor is re-resolved on load; a hash mismatch or a missing file or symbol marks it stale. stale and check list those; path-pin re-anchors one to fresh lines and keeps its note and place in the tree. The agent that changed the code re-pins: repin follows each stale step's text from the parent revision and pins what it can place, printing every change for the agent to check against the note; the rest stays stale for path-pin.

