note Finds the old slice by hash (the match nearest the step's last place when the text repeats), cuts it out with three lines of context, and aligns it with every symbol of the step's name in its file, or in every file once the file or the symbol is gone from it, so a function moved to another file is followed there, keeping the alignment that keeps the most lines. Refuses when no symbol of that name is left anywhere or under half the lines survive: those need someone to read the code.

